Comment: usr/bin/quaff is a statically linked binary.  quaffed itself is
 licensed GPL-3+.  The binary also contains these crates, each under the Expat
 licence: mimalloc 0.1.52 and libmimalloc-sys 0.1.49 (copyright 2019 Octavian
 Oncescu), the latter bundling the mimalloc C library (copyright 2018-2025
 Microsoft Corporation, Daan Leijen).
 .
 It contains these crates, each offered under a choice of licences and used
 here under the Expat licence: ignore 0.4.33, globset 0.4.20, memchr 2.8.3,
 aho-corasick 1.1.5 and walkdir 2.5.0 (copyright 2015 Andrew Gallant),
 same-file 1.0.6 (copyright 2017 Andrew Gallant) and bstr 1.13.1 (copyright
 2018-2019 Andrew Gallant), each Unlicense or Expat, or for bstr Expat or
 Apache-2.0; regex-automata 0.4.18, regex-syntax 0.8.11 and log 0.4.34
 (copyright 2014 The Rust Project Developers), each Expat or Apache-2.0; and
 crossbeam-deque 0.8.8, crossbeam-epoch 0.9.21 and crossbeam-utils 0.8.23
 (copyright 2019 The Crossbeam Project Developers), each Expat or Apache-2.0.
 .
 It contains Ruff's Python parser, under the Expat licence (copyright 2022
 Charles Marsh): ruff_python_ast 0.0.18, ruff_python_parser 0.0.18,
 ruff_python_trivia 0.0.18, ruff_source_file 0.0.18 and ruff_text_size
 0.0.18.  The crates ship no licence file; Ruff's repository licence is Expat,
 and names the projects parts of them are derived from, among them RustPython's
 parser (copyright 2020 RustPython Team, Expat) and rust-analyzer's text-size
 (Expat).  ruff_unicode_names2 0.0.18 (copyright 2014 Huon Wilson), Expat or
 Apache-2.0, used here under Expat, holds tables generated from the Unicode
 Character Database, under the Unicode-DFS-2016 licence (copyright Unicode,
 Inc.).
 .
 It contains these crates under the Expat licence: castaway 0.2.4 (copyright
 2021 Stephen M. Coakley), char_str 0.0.4 (copyright 2024 ryota2357),
 compact_str 0.10.0 (copyright 2021 Parker Timmerman), phf 0.11.3 and
 phf_shared 0.11.3 (copyright 2014-2022 Steven Fackler, Yuki Okushi), and
 zmij 1.0.23 (David Tolnay).
 .
 It contains these crates, each Expat or Apache-2.0 and used here under the
 Expat licence: arrayvec 0.7.8 and itertools 0.15.0 (copyright 2015-2023 Ulrik
 Sverdrup "bluss"), bitflags 2.13.2, libc 0.2.190, rustc-hash 2.1.3 and
 unicode-normalization 0.1.25 (copyright The Rust Project Developers), cfg-if
 1.0.5 (copyright 2014 Alex Crichton), stacker 0.1.25 (copyright 2014 Alex
 Crichton, Simonas Kazlauskas), psm 0.1.32 (copyright 2018 Simonas Kazlauskas),
 drop_bomb 0.1.5 (Aleksey Kladov), either 1.18.0, equivalent 1.0.2, indexmap
 2.14.2 and ordermap 1.2.2 (their developers), get-size2 0.11.0 (copyright 2022
 Denis Kerp, 2025 Nicolas), hashbrown 0.17.1 (copyright 2016 Amanieu d'Antras),
 itoa 1.0.18 and thiserror 2.0.21 (David Tolnay), siphasher 1.0.4 (copyright
 2012-2016 The Rust Project Developers, 2016-2026 Frank Denis), smallvec 1.16.2
 (copyright 2018 The Servo Project Developers), static_assertions 1.1.0
 (copyright 2017 Nikolai Vazquez) and thin-vec 0.2.20 (Aria
 Beingessner).  tinyvec 1.13.3 (copyright 2019 Daniel "Lokathor" Gee) is Zlib,
 Apache-2.0 or Expat, used here under Expat.  ryu 1.0.23 (David Tolnay) is
 Apache-2.0 or BSL-1.0, used here under Apache-2.0.  unicode-ident 1.0.26
 (David Tolnay), Expat or Apache-2.0 and used here under Expat, holds tables
 derived from the Unicode Character Database under the Unicode-3.0 licence
 (copyright 1991-2023 Unicode, Inc.).
 .
 It contains code generated by procedural macros that Ruff's crates use, and
 the crates those macros are built from.  These are each Expat or Apache-2.0,
 used here under the Expat licence: syn 2.0.119, syn 3.0.6, quote 1.0.47,
 rustversion 1.0.23 and thiserror-impl 2.0.21 (David Tolnay), proc-macro2
 1.0.107 (David Tolnay, Alex Crichton), heck 0.5.0 (copyright 2015 The Rust
 Project Developers), get-size-derive2 0.11.0 (copyright 2022 Denis Kerp),
 derive-where 1.7.0 (copyright 2021 Roland Fredenhagen), manyhow-macros 0.11.4
 (copyright 2022 Roland Fredenhagen), interpolator 0.5.0, manyhow 0.11.4 and
 proc-macro-utils 0.10.0 (copyright 2023 Roland Fredenhagen), and
 attribute-derive 0.10.5 (copyright 2024 Roland Fredenhagen).  These are
 Expat: attribute-derive-macro 0.10.5 (copyright 2022 Roland Fredenhagen),
 collection_literals 1.0.3 (copyright The collection_literals Contributors),
 and quote-use 0.8.4 and quote-use-macros 0.8.4, which ship no licence file or
 author; their repository is github.com/ModProg/quote-use.  is-macro 0.3.8
 (강동윤) is Apache-2.0.
 .
 It contains the musl C library
 (copyright 2005-2020 Rich Felker and other contributors), under the Expat
 licence, and the Rust standard library, licensed Expat or Apache-2.0.  It also
 contains LLVM's libunwind, whose licence's LLVM exception waives the notice
 for code embedded in a binary.
 .
 It contains character-mapping tables derived from CPython's codecs, the
 encodings package of Python 3.14.8 (Copyright (c) 2001 Python Software
 Foundation; All Rights Reserved), under the PSF License Version 2.  CPython
 generated those codecs from the Unicode Consortium's mapping files.  The
 change made: each single-byte codec's decoding table, what each run of bytes
 decodes to in each multi-byte codec quaff reads, and the codec and alias
 names, are read from CPython by decoding with it and written out as Rust
 data by scripts/generate-codecs in the source repository, to
 crates/encoding/src/codecs.rs.  Being data in the source tree rather than a
 crate, it is kept here by hand.
 .
 The crates listed here are checked against the binary's dependency graph by
 crates/quaffed/tests/packaging.rs in the source repository.  musl and
 libunwind come with the Rust toolchain rather than as crates, so that test
 cannot see them and they are kept here by hand.

